{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_protocol_tap_protocol", "label": "DevTools tap protocol", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/protocol.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_protocol_single_multiplexed_socket", "label": "One multiplexed WebSocket", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/protocol.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One socket rather than one per panel means a browser tab holds a single connection, switching panels costs no reconnect, and an idle tab costs the system nothing."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_protocol_devtools_protocol_version", "label": "DEVTOOLS_PROTOCOL_VERSION", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/protocol.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Additive changes keep the version and clients must ignore frame kinds, streams and fields they do not recognise - that is what lets an older UI keep working against a newer server. Anything else bumps it, and a mismatch closes the socket with 4400: refusing beats negotiating, because a UI bundle from a different release rendering a half-understood actor tree is worse than a banner telling you to rebuild. The full surface is declared in version 1 from the start so each panel that lands is a pure addition."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_protocol_handshake", "label": "Tap handshake", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/protocol.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The client sends hello first and nothing else is accepted before it; the server answers welcome with the protocol version, server version, system name, start time, streams and panels."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_protocol_capability_advertisement", "label": "Capability advertisement", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/protocol.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A panel is active, disabled because the operator switched it off, or unavailable with a reason - which the UI renders on the greyed-out nav entry, so a capability this system lacks is explained rather than silently missing."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_protocol_tap_streams", "label": "Tap streams", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/protocol.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Subscribing yields a snapshot first then deltas, and the server generates the snapshot on the same mailbox that publishes the deltas so it can never be built from a half-updated view."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_protocol_sequence_numbers", "label": "Per-stream sequence numbers and gaps", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/protocol.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A gap means frames were dropped, so the client incremental state is now a guess: the bundled UI re-subscribes for a fresh snapshot rather than rendering a tree that quietly disagrees with reality. Counters in stream payloads are cumulative since attach, never deltas, so a reconnect or a missed tick cannot corrupt the figures."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_protocol_tap_requests", "label": "Tap request methods", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/protocol.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Pull operations namespaced by the panel that owns them. A method with no handler answers error code unavailable - the same signal the panel descriptor already gave, so a client that ignored the handshake still fails safely. Requests are answered off the tap mailbox so a slow journal read cannot stall other connected tabs."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_protocol_decodeclientframe", "label": "decodeClientFrame", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/protocol.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Rejects anything that is not a well-formed frame, including kinds it does not know: the ignore-what-you-do-not-recognise half of the compatibility rule applies to clients reading server frames, not to the server, which has no reason to accept frames from a client newer than itself."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_protocol_tap_protocol", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_protocol_single_multiplexed_socket", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/protocol.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_protocol_tap_protocol", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_protocol_devtools_protocol_version", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/protocol.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_protocol_tap_protocol", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_protocol_handshake", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/protocol.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_protocol_tap_protocol", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_protocol_capability_advertisement", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/protocol.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_protocol_tap_protocol", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_protocol_tap_streams", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/protocol.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_protocol_tap_protocol", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_protocol_sequence_numbers", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/protocol.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_protocol_tap_protocol", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_protocol_tap_requests", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/protocol.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_protocol_tap_protocol", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_protocol_decodeclientframe", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/protocol.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_protocol_single_multiplexed_socket", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_protocol_tap_protocol", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/protocol.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_protocol_devtools_protocol_version", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_protocol_handshake", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/protocol.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_protocol_capability_advertisement", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_protocol_handshake", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/protocol.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_protocol_sequence_numbers", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_protocol_tap_streams", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/protocol.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_protocol_capability_advertisement", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_protocol_tap_requests", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/devtools/protocol.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_devtools_protocol_decodeclientframe", "target